# Allowlist, deliberately all top-level. The context is the repo root
# (6.7 GB); this keeps only the lockfiles and the entrypoint the build reads.
# The repo itself arrives at runtime as a volume, so no source belongs here.
#
# Every rule is a whole top-level entry on purpose. Nested re-inclusion
# (`!a/b/*.json` after `a/b/*`) is NOT portable: docker re-includes at depth,
# podman does so inconsistently — measured, with both builds succeeding and
# only the file list differing. docker/ and python/ are small enough to admit
# whole, which avoids the question entirely.
*
!.python-version
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!python
!docker
